      "message": "Walk the door and the invitation, and say what a graduation carries\n\nThe first-run walk served one listener, so nothing it proved was\nabout the forge as it is hosted: with the operator's door apart. It\nnow serves the door as the flagship does, does the operator's work\nthere — registering, granting, minting for another, membership,\nquotas, the graduation's account and import — and shows the public\nlistener answering 404 to the same. And it walks the way in that\nphase four built: a stranger asks on the front page, the door lists\nthem, an invitation takes them off the list and signs them in\nexactly once.\n\nThe operating document now says what a graduation does not carry —\npolicy, mirror, tasks, changes and their record, lessons, grants,\ntokens, agents, membership, quota overrides — so an operator moving a\ncompany knows what to set again by hand, and that the receipts verify\nagainst the forge they came from.\n\nServing the walk with a public URL found one more thing: a public\nURL whose host is an address could not start the forge at all, since\na passkey binds to a host name. Such a forge — a LAN, a walk on\nloopback — now runs without passkeys, says so at start-up, and still\nbuilds its links from the URL.\n\nChange-Id: Iwalkdoor0115\nSigned-off-by: Mandip Adhikari <92096340+mandipadk@users.noreply.github.com>",
